{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"A sorted set kept in a splay tree: a binary search tree that rotates each element it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accesses, inserts or removes up to the root (Sleator and Tarjan, 1985).","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/splaytree"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees"]]},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Se","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SE","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"kind":"symbol","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Sorted-sets","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap"],"title":"Sorted sets"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SplayTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A splay tree keeps no balance information. Any sequence of "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" insertions, removals and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accesses on "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" elements costs O(("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") in all, so each takes O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"amortized, and recently or frequently accessed elements stay near the root: accessing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements in ascending order costs O("},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") in all. Reads ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the bounds, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscripts and iteration) leave the tree as it is, so they keep the value semantics and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API of the other sorted sets, and take time proportional to the element’s depth, which a run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of ascending insertions can make "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":". Use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/access(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to look an element up and splay it."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root","recent.contains(25)           \/\/ false, and the tree is unchanged","let parts = recent.split(at: 30)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [10, 20]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [30, 40, 50]"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank like an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array: ","type":"text"},{"code":"tree[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the smallest element. The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"links, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SplayTree"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree.swift#L28","fileName":"SplayTree.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SplayTree","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"BinarySearchTrees"}],"title":"SplayTree","externalID":"s:17BinarySearchTrees9SplayTreeV","symbolKind":"struct"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/Split"],"title":"Structures"},{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifier